@@ -422,6 +422,8 @@ Invoke the captured method synchronously with the already captured frozen descri
 
 The callback may read its completed field and update only the instance's exact still-owned auxiliary presentation. It must not alter author rich DOM, inline data/ownership, canonical data, history, focus/selection/current state or mode, and cannot acquire tasks or nested public/scoped mutation/control authority. Invoke under the existing protected projection/preparation boundary; never hold a guard across an await. No deferred authority, token or scheduling capability is granted. The original-receiver capture and synchronous-result policy from refinement §3.4 applies, including callable thenables and every falsy thrown value.
 
+Poll captures the sanitized readable HTML of a completed option in that option's existing view record. Provider-only result refreshes reuse this completed value under the same exact source/result ownership checks; they do not derive labels from unaccepted author DOM between core completions. The next admitted completion replaces the value, while rebuilding or retiring the author view discards it. This is auxiliary presentation state, not a second canonical store or a field descriptor retained for later delivery.
+
 For Image, derive alt from the final actual caption text. Core proves the field/block owner; Image additionally proves its exact captured image/caption/container/wrapper relationship before writing its auxiliary image. Do not use selectors/closest or a guessed editor ancestor to authorize the write, import renderer parsing into the editor, expand particular inline-plugin payloads manually, or create a canonical no-op action to obtain notification. An image adopted into a foreign container is neither updated nor taken back.
 
 #### Delivery boundaries
